{"id": "EUVD-2026-103722", "enisaUuid": "a9a95398-f953-395c-9cb7-917a702b6734", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: llcp: drop truncated I/RR/RNR PDUs in nfc_llcp_recv_hdlc()\n\nnfc_llcp_recv_hdlc() reads the sequence byte skb->data[2], via\nnfc_llcp_ns()/nfc_llcp_nr(), before any length check. The receive path\nonly guarantees the two-byte LLCP header -- __nfc_llcp_recv() checks it\nwith pskb_may_pull() and nfc_llcp_recv_agf() admits two-byte inner PDUs\n-- so a two-byte I, RR or RNR PDU reads one byte of uninitialised skb\ntailroom. The byte becomes N(R)/N(S); a peer can already set those with\na well-formed PDU, so this is acting on uninitialised memory, not new\npeer control.\n\nGuard the read with pskb_may_pull(), as commit 95674f506c63 (\"nfc: llcp:\nreject PDUs shorter than the LLCP header\") did for the two-byte header,\nso the sequence byte is present and linear before it is read. RR and RNR\nPDUs are LLCP_HEADER_SIZE + LLCP_SEQUENCE_SIZE bytes and an I PDU is\nlonger, so no valid frame is rejected; a truncated PDU is malformed, so\nreturn without a DM reply.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3afdbebfee2ef7e9510880868cfb482cbffe6836", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b4086eb67a9a3b1ce69fef1b6793827363703ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51b6d73373589abb9de4d84767b0db1bc8d395d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/066205553a0106565bcede934f5721c25ebd6e4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18f60ee882403d5b48097f5f6ae45f794e4cc643", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/810f204ef8f61f0c930cf6b3280050b3ee6a8ae7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/744e61bd06188d8bb068c26a461c252f242b05c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/273f9d667cde649f8de9d72b1303cc2f4b658c50"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8vvq-jjhc-wfc4", "CVE-2026-98482"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1232c7d3-88d1-3620-ae58-3f9d4043a901", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "19dce4a6-2453-3aff-b8fe-3374d46e0bf7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d646960f7986fefb460a2b062d5ccc8ccfeacc3a <744e61bd06188d8bb068c26a461c252f242b05c9"}, {"id": "1d7eccaf-5266-374c-8443-9c6e6c40882b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "1e214159-9e75-313a-8fbb-88be815e19ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d646960f7986fefb460a2b062d5ccc8ccfeacc3a <51b6d73373589abb9de4d84767b0db1bc8d395d9"}, {"id": "207a257e-0542-3a4a-b746-0272ca8434b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d646960f7986fefb460a2b062d5ccc8ccfeacc3a <810f204ef8f61f0c930cf6b3280050b3ee6a8ae7"}, {"id": "4d0e9183-3628-3f91-b1d0-9d778d003ecd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "583f36b6-2a7e-3bfd-a49c-553dbb573c93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "623d98ab-c1dc-3110-acff-fd37e5209414", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d646960f7986fefb460a2b062d5ccc8ccfeacc3a <3afdbebfee2ef7e9510880868cfb482cbffe6836"}, {"id": "6843221f-8e75-37bb-851e-85ad19e70615", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "71eb0113-f668-3390-9f31-7a67c1612f6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d646960f7986fefb460a2b062d5ccc8ccfeacc3a <9b4086eb67a9a3b1ce69fef1b6793827363703ce"}, {"id": "80f355ba-2a96-3956-b457-dabbc26f3269", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "98b77edd-e397-38f4-9f67-7e4f888f5f42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "prod